    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 5,
      "versionNonce": 945751377,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "hi-cmthmhbbm4nwp08adg5x82jgs",
      "fillStyle": "hachure",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 50,
      "y": 420,
      "strokeColor": "#000000",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 1125,
      "height": 150,
      "seed": 976874166.7435853,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1788205354385,
      "link": null,
      "locked": true,
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "1. The system should identify clients by user ID, IP address, or API key to apply\nappropriate limits.\n2. The system should limit HTTP requests based on configurable rules (e.g., 100 API requests per\nminute per user).\n3. When limits are exceeded, the system should reject requests with HTTP 429 and include helpful\nheaders (rate limit remaining, reset time).",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. The system should identify clients by user ID, IP address, or API key to apply\nappropriate limits.\n2. The system should limit HTTP requests based on configurable rules (e.g., 100 API requests per\nminute per user).\n3. When limits are exceeded, the system should reject requests with HTTP 429 and include helpful\nheaders (rate limit remaining, reset time).",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "baseline": 144
    },
